                [
                    136.0,
                    1194.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In the evaluation of objective labels (Table 7), the traditional models of BoW+LogReg and fastText+SVM were comparable to the Modal Class baseline. Similar to the evaluation in the subjective labels, the BERT-based models achieved mean absolute errors lower than the Modal Class baseline, and Obj. BERT achieved the highest performance.",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                1216,
                586,
                1407
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 117,
            "global_group_id": 117,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    134.0,
                    1216.0
                ],
                [
                    586.0,
                    1216.0
                ],
                [
                    586.0,
                    1407.0
                ],
                [
                    134.0,
                    1407.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Below the dotted line in Table 7, the performance of the human readers is shown for comparison. Note that the objective labels are the average of each of these readers. Compared to each reader, Obj. BERT does not reach human performance.",
